"dia_id":"D20:7","global_turn_index":341,"locator":"[S20T7]","raw_turn_sha256":"02447cc496b3c4f749ca64410d4c57c56e8282398ce8fb5a96f31076904b440f","rendered_turn_sha256":"577323732c407ed0683deb783063f1470a7914c498795d3eb2a53777ac25a5cf","session_date":"2023-09-22","session_datetime":"2023-09-22T20:57:00","session_id":"session_20","session_index":20,"source_sha256":"fff200ee60d7c4e90e8796280e8ff82807fc8c9db2d16dabe488b7c33fc6b9e3","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":7}],"speaker":null,"store_id":"s1","store_snapshot_sha256":"ca39361e8e23f204a9fda55fc83e3ce7f411c7c8d582939aa63688c1923c7679","text":"Dave: Wow, Calvin, that's awesome! That feeling of freedom in the summer is the best. A moment of reflection not only makes the journey interesting but also productive! Hey, any songs from your childhood that bring back memories?\n[S20T5] (dia_id: D20:5)\n\nCalvin: Yeah, there's this one song that always makes me smile. It played during a road trip with my dad and we had so much fun singing along to it.\n[S20T6] (dia_id: D20:6)\n\nDave: Sounds awesome, Calvin! Road trips with family are always a treat. What's the name of the song?\n[S20T7] (dia_id: D20:7)","text_sha256":"a83e2e4dd9e549209218882ad1c8dcb030982984fba3fc3f0dfd78ac9c9b0aa1","timestamp":"2023-09-22T20:57:00"},{"attribution_index_sha256":"08302ae53c7681312a62f5734d6ef73dfd8c86405ba319838bd79230cce094d2","attribution_units":[{"dia_ids":["D22:5"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":28,"line_start":27,"source_locators":["[S22T5]"],"text_sha256":"1a4bb4e5e3813ac263f857847d17b16c435017bddad1d4cd221ef7b81c61324e"}],"dia_ids":["D22:5"],"evidence_id":"ev-44dc606f5f7d00b35be0f581f7a773f6e21a940efeb87b6764cac1a9b9d84da0","group_id":"session_22","line_end":28,"line_start":27,"observation_ids":["obs-0006"],"path":"/memories/session-22.md","query_terms":[],"rank":null,"records_sha256":"130a5a1e1b75083358ef27a98dd215a4e75c819ace6f2ee9b560ba394e0f0394","retrieval_round":9,"schema_version":1,"score":null,"section":"# Session 22","selection_ordinal":4,"session_id":"session_22","source_kind":"raw","source_locators":["[S22T5]"],"source_map_sha256":"6e99115961bae06a48bfb7e82dbdcc18dc32ccf6c5ce57e3c266dfc7a5d4d574","source_records":[{"dia_id":"D22:5","global_turn_index":374,"locator":"[S22T5]","raw_turn_sha256":"d9df745e960a9235c8ef6144815906d4e022abaaa2b260446481c487ba842026","rendered_turn_sha256":"1a4bb4e5e3813ac263f857847d17b16c435017bddad1d4cd221ef7b81c61324e","session_date":"2023-10-08","session_datetime":"2023-10-08T15:13:00","session_id":"session_22","session_index":22,"source_sha256":"21025906b21bb4f66753338fae54c39b0c8d7507b31852bdc3645a6571e8e0b0","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":5}],"speaker":"Dave","store_id":"s1","store_snapshot_sha256":"ca39361e8e23f204a9fda55fc83e3ce7f411c7c8d582939aa63688c1923c7679","text":"Dave: Thanks Calvin! I've spent a lot of time and effort on it. It's not just a hobby, it's a passion. It's like therapy, a way to get away from everyday stress. When I was little I'd spend hours in my dad's garage, tinkering with engines - it was like my own sanctuary. Now I'm lucky enough to do this as a job, to take something broken and make it into something awesome.\n[S22T5] (dia_id: D22:5)","text_sha256":"1a4bb4e5e3813ac263f857847d17b16c435017bddad1d4cd221ef7b81c61324e","timestamp":"2023-10-08T15:13:00"},{"attribution_index_sha256":"08302ae53c7681312a62f5734d6ef73dfd8c86405ba319838bd79230cce094d2","attribution_units":[{"dia_ids":["D26:6"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":29,"line_start":28,"source_locators":["[S26T6]"],"text_sha256":"b775c33f1cef75ef7013961b39fd3d6f5585cda8a8f835ce1daefaf0b8bae756"}],"dia_ids":["D26:6"],"evidence_id":"ev-1be17f9909b301038ed28cb24d42c902a25c40ccf903e7d0b572a7b876eb022a","group_id":"session_26","line_end":29,"line_start":28,"observation_ids":["obs-0007"],"path":"/memories/session-26.md","query_terms":[],"rank":null,"records_sha256":"130a5a1e1b75083358ef27a98dd215a4e75c819ace6f2ee9b560ba394e0f0394","retrieval_round":9,"schema_version":1,"score":null,"section":